I cannot provide a simple "Yes" or "No" answer to this question, as whether driving is the better commute choice depends on multiple variable factors that are specific to your situation, such as:
- The distance of your commute and the availability, reliability, and convenience of alternative commute options like public transport, cycling, or walking;
- Associated costs including fuel, vehicle maintenance, parking fees, potential tolls, versus the costs of other commute methods;
- Local traffic conditions which can affect travel time, stress levels, and fuel consumption;
- Environmental concerns you may have regarding carbon emissions from driving;
- Your personal needs such as carrying work equipment, having flexible travel times, or accommodating personal errands before/after work.

You can evaluate these specific factors relevant to your circumstances to determine the most suitable commute choice for you.
